{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1043947-the-driftwood-incident\u2014a-chronicle-report","id":1043947,"title":"The Driftwood Incident\u2014a Chronicle report","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-05T06:27:53-08:00","id":1043947,"title":"The Driftwood Incident\u2014a Chronicle report","content":"My Chronicle (full title \u201cThe Driftwood Incident and What Came After\u201d) was inspired by the Southern Reach Trilogy by Jeff Vandermeer. I strongly recommend these books if you like weird science fiction. <br /> <br /> A strange, impenetrable region has emerged in the forests of rural Florida. It is bafflingly resistant to sphere magick. There is only one way in. Inside, it is nature gone amok. The town it has subsumed is overrun with vines and impossibly fast plant growth. Giant mutant wildlife is everywhere. <br /> <br /> The zone proves difficult to explore. Scientific instruments read weird, inconsistent results. Recording devices bring back nothing but static. Casualties among the Void Engineer explorers are high. Even those who survive expeditions are changed by it. Increasingly, the Union finds zone expeditions a distraction and waste of resources. (Requisitions Background? Backup? Nope. Sorry; budget cuts.)<br /> <br /> The problem is, the phenomenon is growing. Nothing seems to stop it and it threatens to swallow the whole world if left unchecked. <br /> <br /> As an act of desperation, the Driftwood Institute, the amalgam formed for and tasked with researching the phenomenon, is forced to seek help from some contracted \u201cconsultants\u201d\u2014a group of Tradition mages. If the Union finds out who the consultants are it would be considered an act of treason, but this may be the only way to save the world. <br /> <br /> Spoilers in this thread, so Larry, Larry, Joe, Charli, and Richard\u2014get out!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:28:39-08:00","id":1043948,"title":"","content":"<br /> If you\u2019ve read <i>Southern Reach Trilogy</i> by Jeff Vandermeer, you\u2019ll recognize my Driftwood Institute as the \u201cS\u00e9ances and Science Brigade\u201d from that series. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve made some changes to the Mage canon that make this setting possible. First, the Avatar Storm hit the Technocratic Union much more severely here than in the official canon. The Pogrom actually stopped while the Union regained their bearings, giving the Traditions (those who survived the Avatar Storm) some room to breathe. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy simply don\u2019t have the numbers to hunt down supernaturals the way they used to. In fact, a lot of the control mechanisms that used to be in place have slipped. They still have a Timetable and an agenda for controlling the world, and still keep up the trappings of an all-powerful conspiracy, but they currently lack the manpower and mat\u00e9riel to keep up a global organization that controls the world. <br /> <br /> And that has resulted in a shift in the Consensus.<br /> <br /> In 2017, we live in a post-factual world. The un-Enlightened are increasingly resistant to facts. Many people no longer even believe that empirical Truth exists at all. It\u2019s not that people believe in magick instead of science\u2014it\u2019s that many people just don\u2019t believe in anything. <br /> Technocratic effects are increasingly generating paradox more than at any time since the Order of Reason began. The Conventions are starting to freak out and turn on each other. The NWO and Iteration X are at odds with the Syndicate and Progenitors. Void Engineers are caught in the middle. It's a highly-charged political minefield. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 02-05-2017, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:46:39-08:00","id":1043958,"title":"","content":"Core Themes:<br /> <br /> <b>Post-factualism</b> and its effect on the Consensus.<br /> <b>Environmental threats</b> and how they are prioritized (or not). The weird zone is a metaphor for global warming.<br /> <b>Prejudice and racial violence</b>. This is a crossover campaign with Changeling and the Autumn People and Dauntain are problems in the outside world. Hate crimes against changelings are happening more and more. Unseelie Redcaps (Make America Great Again) are rioting in the streets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T01:28:30-08:00","id":1045652,"title":"","content":"Ooh, this'll be a good read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6010-shadowstep6","name":"Shadowstep6","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:35:07-08:00","id":1046244,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Dramatis Personae</b></i><br /> (I'd have more to post here if the players would get off their asses and finish and post their character sheets to the Facebook group like they're supposed to.)<br /> <br /> <b>Karen Reiner</b> (NPC)\u2014Void Engineer, Research &amp; Execution<br /> Karen is director of the Driftwood Institute, the research amalgam created to investigate Incident 2014H31 (Codename &quot;Driftwood&quot;). The mundane front for the Institute is a climate change research non-profit headquartered in Tallahassee. Karen is a weather researcher and I'm keeping her magick under wraps until such time as I can surprise the PCs by her calling a lightning bolt out of a cloud at something.<br /> <br /> <b>Kia</b> (Bryan)\u2014Order of Hermes, House Xaos<br /> Kia and Karen became Awakened together as grad students. They were close friends and confidants, but as Kia explored the boundaries of his paradigm through increasingly chaotic practices, including mind-expanding drugs and tantra, Karen found that wasn't doing anything for her and they gradually grew apart. Eventually, he ended up joining House Thig and she dropped off the map into the Technocracy. She looked him up again when she got the idea to bring mysticks in as consultants. Kia is a master of sensory magicks in a lot of Spheres, is a skilled Investigator, occult expert, and cryptologist.<br /> Bryan is the reason this whole Chronicle exists.<br /> <br /> <b>Arnold Lane</b> (Larry)\u2014Void Engineers, Research &amp; Execution<br /> Arnold is based on Val Kilmer's character from Real Genius. Larry has made it clear that he wants an ambitious character who is looking for promotions up the ladder, but Arnold is going to have to work on his social skills if he's going to successfully do that. I'm building into the story arc some situations where he can take over from Karen as director, but then he'll be stuck dealing with crap he doesn't know she's been shielding him from. Arnold is the Correspondence master and will be interacting with the party a lot via holograms of himself and co-location. He doesn't like getting dirty.<br /> <br /> <b>Dan</b> (NPC)\u2014Extraordinary Citizen<br /> Larry took dots in Allies so Dan is Arnold's intern. Dan has 0 Arete, but Genius 2, so his Eidolon could Awaken at some point. Until then, he's using his G.I. Bill money to get a master's degree in engineering and earning college credit by being a badass in this amalgam.<br /> <br /> <b>Professor Dick A Philip III </b>&quot;Dap3&quot; (the other Larry)\u2014Cult of Ecstasy<br /> When I was describing the setting, Larry asked me &quot;Wait, can I play Terrence McKenna in this?&quot; &quot;That sounds perfect.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Robert</b> (Richard)\u2014 Order of Hermes, House Ngoma<br /> What I've gotten from Richard so far is he wants his character to be born in America, but got deeply into exploring his roots back in Africa. When he pitched the character\u2014he was the last person to ask to join the playgroup after my setting planning was well underway\u2014I was a little worried (how am I going to work this in?) but he specifically asked for a Order of Hermes Ngoma, not a Disparate Ngoma, so I'm pretty confident I can fit him in as a colleague of Kia's.<br /> <br /> <b>Grover</b> (Joe)\u2014Progenitors, Pharmacopeists<br /> Joe has a history of playing goofy characters who do wild, unpredictable things and here he's playing a Doctor Moreau-type biological researcher. Because it's Joe, he's going to find himself addicted to something inside the zone that he can't replicate in the lab (spoiler: because it's faerie glamour) and this is the hook to get Larry's Ecstasy Cultist in the amalgam.<br /> <br /> <b>Oliver</b> (Charli)\u2014Iteration X<br /> Oliver is a cyborg with a camouflage implant. He was the lone survivor of the first expedition inside the anomaly. Now he's working for Driftwood as a programmer, but his skills as an asskicker will be needed soon enough. His personal research interests are programming compassion into artificial intelligences. Oliver has broken his social conditioning and Karen doesn't care. He desperately doesn't want to be reassigned back to another unit where he'll be made back into a soldier. <br /> <br /> <b>0fe1:a</b> &quot;Ofelia&quot; (NPC)\u2014Familiar/Companion<br /> 0fel:a is a free AI and Oliver's familiar. She lives in a handheld tablet, but can also reside in his brain, or out on the web. We don't know her story yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 04-01-2017, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:14:11-08:00","id":1052950,"title":"","content":"First game is on the playgroup's calendar\u2014March 5th. <br /> <br /> Yay!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T06:49:09-08:00","id":1055214,"title":"","content":"Oh, I forgot that I did this. I shared it with the players already as a prelude to the first session. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> (Since I can't attach an image, see <a href=\"https://twitter.com/golgariglenross/status/835863499599380480\" target=\"_blank\">the spread here</a>.)</span></span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/golgariglenross/status/835863499599380480\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/golgariglenross/status/835863499599380480\" target=\"_blank\"> Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/golgariglenross/status/835863499599380480\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/golgariglenross/status/835863499599380480 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This post is from a protected account. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Center: Five of <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Patterns</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2022 Sunday: The Mage</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2022 Monday: Seven of Patterns<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2022 Tuesday: Gaia (reversed)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2022 Wednesday: Ace of Dynamism</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2022 Thursday: Two of Questing</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2022 Friday: Two of Primordialism</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2022 Saturday: The Hierophant<br /> <br /> This spread was totally random, but it follows Karen's path quite closely and explains the start of the Cabal/Amalgam merger. <br /> <br /> Karen is greatly concerned (5 of Pattern, in the Thoth deck this card is called &quot;Worry&quot;). Her mission isn't going well. She realizes this and knows she must act (The Mage). What they've been doing to control the singularity isn't effective. She must step outside of her comfort zone in order to proceed, which is frightening (7 of Patterns, which in Thoth is the &quot;Failure&quot; card) It's too early in the spread to be a conclusion of failure, simply that attempts at a quick resolution have not borne fruit. This is an Earth card, which often means something material. The Union has cancelled everyone's Backup and Requisitions backgrounds. No help is coming from the Union. <br /> <br /> The Universe (Gaia) in its reversed form reiterates this: spinning her wheels, not getting results. Literal interpretation is the world is upside-down. </span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> But then, a breakthrough. The Ace of Dynamism represents the potential of an idea. What if we don't go to the Union for help? Maybe, she thinks, we could reach out to the Traditions? She's had this idea for a while, but she's pushed it away. The time for decisive action has come (2 of Questing, which is explicitly a card about the Order of Hermes). <br /> <br /> The spread concludes with increasing harmony within the united cabal (2 of Cups) and the culmination of efforts toward Karen's increasing wisdom and leadership (Hierophant).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:26:58-08:00","id":1055304,"title":"","content":"What are your plans for next moves? Do you need any help planning your Chronicle?<br /> <br /> Well, since you're putting techies and trads toghether, they'll prabably need a common external danger that is bigger than both to keep their bound.<br /> <br /> That's were the Nefandi steps in.<br /> <br /> Also, will you be using the Changelling from the Lost, as a sort of new kind of critter, or just changellings from the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> You could use some True Fae seeking to create a new legend for itself as one main antagonistic force. Some macabre, twisted destruction force working as the current encarnation of this True Fae for this legend, maybe with an avatar actor as the Grim Reaper or the Angel of Death or something like it.<br /> <br /> This True Fae could be working to progressively expand the opening, as a plot to lure would-be heroes into the tale it needs so much for its continued existence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T22:01:25-08:00","id":1056979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1043947-the-driftwood-incident\u2014a-chronicle-report?p=1055304#post1055304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need any help planning your Chronicle?<br /> [\u2026]<br /> This True Fae could be working to progressively expand the opening, as a plot to lure would-be heroes into the tale it needs so much for its continued existence</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of that angle, but it works. It works soooo good. It actually explains something I'll get to in a bit. <br /> <br /> While I don't <i>need</i> help, every comment I've gotten on this forum is making the story better and I appreciate you all for it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:39:29-08:00","id":1059241,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Season 1, Episode 0</b><br /> <br /> <i>Act 1</i><br /> Tonight\u2019s session opened in Jacksonville Florida. Arnold (Void Engineers) and Grover (Progenitors) with their director Karen (Void Engineers NPC) are making an appearance on Science Friday with Ira Flatow as part of their outreach to promote the Technocratic paradigm. This is clearly necessary because they field three particularly hostile and ignorant callers challenging basic science. Arnold blows his cover then saves himself with a joke (Charisma+Subterfuge). Grover fumbles an answer (roleplayed, no roll) and gets interrupted by Karen, who bails him out. These are probably not the surrogates that the Technocratic Union wants to be promoting their agenda on live radio.<br /> <i>Act 1 Scene 2</i><br /> On the way out of the studio, they\u2019re met with a throng of anti-vaxx, climate-change denier protestors (one of the callers was from the International Church of the Holy Rapture of Fort Worth Texas and was calling from the parking lot). Arnold goes into the men\u2019s room, teleports to the car, and drives it on the sidewalk to pick up Grover and Karen.<br /> Karen brings them to the Mayo Clinic in Jacksonville (a Technocracy-affiliated hospital) where four survivors of the last expedition are in intensive care with an untreatable skin condition. Grover reads their charts, Karen has a meeting in a conference room that the PCs are not privy to, Arnold waited in the car because he DGAF.<br /> <i>Act 1 Scene 3</i><br /> They return to their base in Tallahassee. Grover\u2019s DNA sequencing on the biological samples has finished in his absence. The data is total, unreadable garbage. The sample is a fruit of unknown species. Gordon considers eating the fruit, but doesn\u2019t and feeds another slice of it to some rats. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(This comes as a total surprise to me, as Gordon\u2019s player Joe is all about reckless acts like eating an unknown sample. We skip the scene I had prepared where he has a 5-hour hallucinogenic Glamour trip.)</span><br /> <br /> <i>Act 2 Scene 1</i><br /> Meanwhile, Professor Dick Albert Philip III (Cult of Ecstasy) (Dap3 on the Internet) is doing some online browsing and finds a forum post from Grover asking if anyone can identify the species of fruit he\u2019s investigating. He is stunned by this post\u2014it\u2019s a goblinfruit, a glamour-infused manifestation that comes from the Maya/Dreamrealms. How can it be stable enough for a scientist to have it? They exchange emails and exchange Intelligence+Investigation rolls about one another and are immediately smitten with one another.<br /> Arnold monitors their conversation, (as does a NWO NPC, but they don\u2019t know this).<br /> <i>Act 2 Scene 2</i><br /> On his way home from his campus office, Dick encounters three children around age 10. Two bullies, one of whom is wearing a red trucker\u2019s cap that says \u201cMake America Great Again,\u201d push a third child into a puddle. They\u2019re picking on him for being a \u201cfurry.\u201d He\u2019s wearing a headband with fuzzy fox ears on it.<br /> Dick\u2019s Perception+Awareness roll botches, so the rest of this encounter is perfectly mundane, apart from the child in the Make America Great Again hat scoring four successes on an Intimidate roll against a grown man, stealing a book out of his hands and biting it in half. Nothing unusual at all.<br /> <br /> <i>Act 3</i><br /> We then had a brief scene explaining how Robert (Order of Hermes, House Ngoma) ended up drawing the ire of a Russian oil billionaire, prompting his return to the relative safety of the United States.<br /> Robert is a social scientist studying the African diaspora populations. Robert is currently living near a community of Zimbabwean refugees. Things in 2017 aren't good for refugees. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(I wasn't aware of this detail until we were in the middle of roleplay, so I didn't have time to think of this until the day after, but the refugees' community is right in the path of the growing singularity, and they will be tragically forced to move again, explaining Robert's involvement in the cabal). </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":".  adding details, correcting errors 03-10-2017, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:49:19-08:00","id":1059272,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Act 4</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Flashback to the Driftwood Incident of 2014. This is where it all began. I gave everyone except for Oliver (Iteration X)'s player temporary character sheets\u2014blatant redshirts. The players immediately realized they shouldn\u2019t get attached to these characters.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In 2014 category 5 Hurricane Isaias made landfall on the Florida panhandle. Shortly afterwards, a spatial anomaly was detected. A Search &amp; Recovery squad of Void Engineers and Iteration X cyborgs were deployed to extract Technocracy personnel. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Several clues were revealed before the end of the scene. First, there is a gap in the event horizon that can be located with Correspondence 1, but only if you\u2019re looking directly for it, you don\u2019t passively get it through Correspondence Sight. Second, the survivor in the Technocracy lab was working on a machine and fought his rescuers in order to recover a component from it. It was still in his pocket when they escaped. Third, nature is going nuts in there and sensory Effects don\u2019t seem to be working properly (Life 1 Sight didn\u2019t detect the grass growing fast enough to entrap their legs, for example). Finally, the telepath was overcome by a voice on the wind and lost control of his mind. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">We didn\u2019t play all the way to the end of the TPK, but it was clearly inevitable. The captain of the squad was killed by a flock of angry pelicans. Another was entrapped by rapidly growing weeds. The cyborg with the plasma cannon arm was getting up in Paradox, so the first botch would have killed him. Finally, the communications officer botched a Willpower roll and rebroadcast the voice in the telepath\u2019s head full strength into everyone\u2019s mind. Game over, man! </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charli made a couple of very smart decisions that led to Oliver being the lone survivor without my having to fudge anything. He takes the scientist survivor that they rescued and helps him, retreating to the portal rather than fight the numerous hostiles. He also got 4 Willpower successes to resist the voice in his mind. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(I was prepared to cheat a lot to make him the lone survivor but didn\u2019t have to.)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">On his way out, Oliver goes to find the gap in the event horizon and discovers his navigation device is lost! In an act of desperation or flash of Inspiration, he runs the Effect without the device\u2014something a Technocrat should not be able to do. This is a secret that he\u2019s kept since that day, since if anyone found out he was a Reality Deviant, he\u2019d probably be Room 101\u2019d and dissected. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Later, when he meets the debriefing team investigating the Incident, he asks to join the team where he\u2019s been ever since. He\u2019s broken his social conditioning and Karen at Driftwood Institute doesn\u2019t seem to care. He desperately doesn\u2019t want to go back to his old unit. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 03-10-2017, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:53:08-08:00","id":1059765,"title":"","content":"And in some chat-based side-roleplay, Arnold (Void Engineers)'s player has indicated that he is feeling somewhat NWO and wishes to act as a mole, reporting back to the Union that his supervisor and colleagues are trafficking with Reality Deviants. Also, he told me his long-term plans for the character which are, to be blunt, <i>evil</i>. <br /> <br /> I'd already decided that the upper management of the Union were Nephandi. I hadn't planned on this taking as direct a role, (it explains why they were neglecting actively dealing with the singularity, but I wasn't planning on this campaign being about cultists) but now it's definitely coming front and center with regards to this one character. <br /> <br /> Arnold is being groomed as a future barabbi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T07:41:42-07:00","id":1061539,"title":"","content":"Side roleplay:<br /> <b>Karen</b> (Void Engineer NPC) has a staff meeting with all of the Technocracy staff reporting that there will be no more support from the Union. No more marines from the Void Engineers or Iteration X to conduct expeditions, meaning any more explorations will have to be conducted by the scientists themselves. No more equipment requisitions will be approved, so they're stuck with only the tools and equipment already in the building. They have about 6 months of operating expenses left from last year's grant. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(This isn't really roleplay, but plot fiat. I told the players about this way back when we were making characters, which is why none of the Technocracy PCs have any dots in Backup, Requisitions, or Secret Weapons). </span><br /> <br /> <b>Arnold</b> (Void Engineers)'s player initiated a chat with me on Facebook declaring that he is going to send details about Grover and Karen's contact with Traditions mages to Control via an Internet Dead Drop. He assumes that the dead drop is going to the Good Guys. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(GM note: LOL)</span> He also picked up on the possible faerie connection from the email exchange and started researching. The Void Engineers have no good observational data on faerie, but lots of folklore.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I posted on the game Facebook page a reminder that Nephandi are not playable PCs and he insisted in chat that he's NOT looking at joining the Nephandi. I asked if that was Larry talking or Arnold's hitherto unseen moral core, and he said he hadn't thought too much about it. In Arnold's character concept and initial couple of roleplay sessions, I can see three separate, effective ways of tempting him to becoming a barabbi. I'll have to make sure to work in several moral decision points where he can choose to be a hero. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Robert</b> (Order of Hermes, House Ngoma) is a social scientist doing an ethnography of Zimbabwean diaspora. There's a pocket of refugees who have settled comfortably and are doing quite well in North Florida, but they've been approached by a man in a black suit (Mr. Glass) talking about moving them. This would be stressful under any circumstances, but fear and distrust of the government amongst refugees right now is very high (Trump is President in my game world, too). Robert argues on their behalf, but the men in black are quite insistent. Later, Karen meets with Robert, straight-up admits the cover story is a lie, and invites him to come see for himself why they need to evacuate their community. To be continued next session. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I'm not sure where I'm going with this, actually. If they go with the Men in Black, they'll be resettled in a safe community; if they wait for the actual cops to evacuate them, they might be deported.</span><br /> <br /> Behind the scenes, the infosec director of Driftwood, Mr. Glass, tells Karen about <b>Grover</b> (Progenitors)'s communication with a known member of the Cult of Ecstasy (i.e., <b>Dick</b>) . Karen tells Grover to call Dick and invite him to come down to Florida.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The NPC character of Mr. Glass has changed considerably since my original campaign design. Originally, he was a MiB reporting everything back to the NWO, but since Arnold is now acting as the hidden mole in the organization, I've decided that Mr. Glass is a member of the Harbingers of Avalon. </span><br /> <br /> Next session is on the 19th. They will be going inside the event horizon into the Zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T21:23:24-07:00","id":1065087,"title":"","content":"<b>Episode 1: Act 1, Leftovers from last session</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(Oliver's player is out of town)</span><br /> <br /> Scene 1:<br /> The three mystic mages, <b>Robert</b> (Order of Hermes, Ngoma), <b>Kia</b> (Order of Hermes, Xaos), and <b>Dick</b> (Cult of Ecstasy), are invited by the Driftwood Institute to come to visit Florida. They agree to this for a variety of personal reasons (see above).<br /> <br /> Their first encounter with the singularity is a measurement ritual that <b>Arnold</b> (Void Engineers) conducts which involves a surveyor's transit, a bundle of grade-stakes, flagging tape, and a 300' tape measure (those are the foci for a Correspondence Procedure). The three mages along with Dan (Extraordinary Citizen, Void Engineers, Intern) are to place a stake every 300' walking through a grassy marsh flat toward the river, but somehow they never seem to be getting closer to the river. Space is fractal here and the earth has infinite surface area within a finite volume. There is no way to walk through the event horizon as it keeps retreating. Kia is able to detect the event horizon with his mystical senses of Correspondence and Dick can feel the time-shear of the event horizon with Time sphere sensory effect\u2014something it took the Technocracy months to properly analyze.<br /> <br /> This is basically &quot;hazing the new guys&quot; by Arnold, as he knows perfectly well that the event horizon can't be walked through in that way. The result of the ritual is that the phenomenon has grown only a few centimeters since the last time he measured it. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">At this point Arnold's player spent about a half hour posing &quot;what if&quot; questions about the event horizon that I wasn't fully prepared for. I started at this point to worry the session would run late. Eventually I have to GM fiat &quot;that's enough&quot; which I feel kinda bad about since he's genuinely interested in figuring out the mystery. </span><br /> <br /> Scene 2:<br /> <b>Dick</b> (Cult of Ecstasy) and <b>Grover</b> (Progenitor, Pharmacopeist) chat in the marsh flat about the mysterious fruit. They agree to go back to the lab to investigate (i.e., eat) it.<br /> At the lab, Mr Glass (NPC, New World Order, secretly Harbingers of Avalon) tells Grover absolutely under no circumstances is Dick\u2014a known member of the Traditions\u2014allowed in the lab. (He's had the argument with Karen (Void Engineers) about their participation in missions already, but he's holding firm on security of their headquarters). Grover rolls Manipulation to persuade and beat's Glass's Willpower roll and so Glass agrees to a Visitor Pass that allows him in the lobby and the conference room, but not into the lab itself. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Glass could have beaten this, but I forgot to bring his character sheet and I kinda wanted to see it play out so I just did a straight opposed Manipulation+Subterfuge vs Willpower and Grover won it fair-and-square.</span><br /> <br /> Karen wipes hand sanitizer over the camera lens as Brenda (Extraordinary Citizen, Syndicate, office secretary) take a photo for his visitor badge so that the picture is too blurry to really identify him.<br /> <br /> They eat the goblin fruit. This Enchants them both. Dick freaks out at the oppressive Banality inside the Technocracy facility. Grover suddenly realizes everything makes sense and he goes back to the lab to retrieve the ruined DNA results of the biological samples. It is actually a poem! He dictates it to Brenda, who patiently transcribes it. Dick has to get the hell out of here, goes outside and talks to a tree (dryad) on the other side of the parking lot for three hours. He meets a satyr, briefly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This was a really fun scene to roleplay, but my players clearly have waaaay more experience taking drugs than I have so if Glamour trips are going to continue to be a thing, I'm going to need to brainstorm some more stuff to say about them. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The rest of the episode tomorrow. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 03-20-2017, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T17:48:48-07:00","id":1065521,"title":"","content":"<b>Episode 1, Act 2, Expedition A</b><br /> <br /> It's time to go through the breach through the event horizon into the mysterious zone. The Technocracy is no longer assigning marines to do their missions, so the scientists are stuck doing this themselves now. The mission requires them to go and get the &quot;telemetry signal repeater&quot; which is the spellcasting focus for <b>Arnold</b> (Void Engineer)'s Correspondence sensory Effects, repair it, and redeploy it. It was destroyed in the last expedition in a &quot;sudden weather event.&quot;<br /> <br /> The twist is that Karen (Void Engineer) has ordered them to <i>avoid using force at all costs</i>. She has a hypothesis that she wants to collect data on. No weapon use on hostiles unless necessary. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I want to make it clear to the players that this isn't something they can defeat with weapons and that violence is self-defeating.</span><br /> <br /> <i><u>Scene 1</u></i><br /> The team goes through on foot. They are in the same grassy estuary as before but this time there is no spatial effect blocking them from walking toward the river. <b>Dick</b> (Cult of Ecstasy) uses Time perception (focus: marijuana and old-style 3D glasses) to see the time shear between outside and inside. <b>Kia</b> (Order of Hermes, Xaos) uses his own Correspondence perception (sunglasses with sigils on them) to see the fractal bending. This is something the Technocracy took months to fully map out.<br /> <br /> <b>Robert</b> (Order of Hermes, Ngoma) uses his Spirit 1 sensory effect (focus: a lens) to look for spirits. The place is full of spirits and the Gauntlet is completely non-existent; any umbrood they see will be physically manifested. He rolls Perception well and notices something I'd been planning to surprise him with: tiny, tiny chigger spirits trying to bite him. They latch onto him and start to bite and he uses Spirit 2 to negotiate with them. The chigger spirits don't say much (&quot;Hungry!&quot; &quot;Cold!&quot; etc.), but only Robert can hear them.<br /> <b>Grover</b> (Progenitors, Pharmacopeist) also misses his save against their grapple and is likewise covered in chiggers. He tries treating them with his own, normal medical methods, which only causes him health levels of bashing damage. Robert manages a few successes on a Manipulation+Intimidation roll over a few turns and the chigger spirits botch their roll to hang on and fall off.<br /> Looking at this from Arnold and Dan's point of view\u2014a crazy guy got bugs on him and he talked to them and made them go away. They flee the grassy field before the rest of them get bitten and then Robert repeats the Effect on Grover, saving him from the chiggers burrowing under his skin and masticating his flesh from the inside out. Grover recognizes (Intelligence+Medicine) that this is what happened to the Void Engineer marines in the hospital.<br /> <br /> <i><u>Scene 2</u></i><br /> They walk into a forest of red pine that once was a town. The buildings are grown over with vines, whole adult trees are growing through the pavement. They come upon what looks like a tornado struck, there's a swath of fallen trees and stripped roofs. They find the house they're looking for where the marines had previously set up the signal repeater. There's a tree across the porch and they cannot access the door. Intern Dan (Void Engineer Extraordinary Citizen) climbs a tree and drops into a hole in the roof. Kia tries, botches, and falls on his ass for 1 bashing damage. Dan rolls one success to disassemble the device then on his next roll botches and yells for help. Arnold insults him. Dan gets pissed off and shoots the plywood off a downstairs window with his door-breaching gun (an Enlightened Device). Arnold reluctantly goes inside to help him and rolls 6 successes on his first roll (Intelligence+Technology).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Dick finds two more of the mysterious fruit growing on a tree (he rolled four successes). Grover tries to take a sample branch to graft and root sample to cultivate. He botches, probably killing the tree.<br /> <br /> Kia, Karen, and Robert discover they are being watched. They see a man in a tattered feathered cloak and grand headdress. Robert rolls Intelligence+Occult for the second-longest chain of 10-agains I have ever seen and recognizes him\u2014it's Hurakan, the Mayan god of storms.<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"> I'd intended this to be a research roll later in downtime, but that was one crazy roll. </span><br /> Arnold is a wiseass and quotes Ghostbusters, &quot;As duly appointed representative of the City, County and State of New York, I order you to cease andy and all supernatural activity and return forthwith to your place of origin or the next convenient parallel dimension.&quot;<br /> <br /> But if he could, don't you think he would?<br /> <br /> <i><u>Scene 3</u></i><br /> Hurakan is <i>maaaaad</i>. Spirits have Rage, but this was RAGE. Robert negotiates with him with Spirit 2 and some friendly talk and Dick tries reading his mind with Mind 3 (that doesn't work). Arnold looks to Karen for what to do next and she indicates that he should wait because this is what they brought the mystics along for.<br /> After a minute, Hurakan's demeanor changes. He gets up, appears to go from rage to fear, and flees, conjuring a wind gale to ride.<br /> This creates a problem as trees start falling. Dexterity+Athletics rolls for everyone! Except for Dick. Dick instead tries to strengthen his telepathic bond with Hurakan to ask him to come back and doesn't dodge the tree that falls directly on him for 3 damage. Dan also misses his roll and isn't injured, but his way is blocked. Grover, however, rolls 6 successes to dodge a piece of the roof flying at him in an act of John Woo aerial wirework. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Somehow in all of this no one thinks to use Forces to help them dodge the falling debris. </span><br /> <br /> They hear voices coming out of the forest. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is what Hurakan was fleeing. They don't know this yet</span>.<br /> <br /> Grover botches his Willpower roll to avoid his mind being taken by the voices and has a seizure. Dick uses some of the drugs in Grover's own medkit on Grover as a focus for Mind 3 to restore his mind. The group flees the forest before they lose any more to the voices.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Scene 4</i></u><br /> Brief scene. They easily resist the chiggers in the field again. Near the gateway is a giant alligator but from the belly to the tail it has the body of a giant squid. It is not made of manifested ephemera, not a spirit. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(They don't know this, it's a wyrd chimera.) </span>Dick again saves the day by sending a mental impulse to it causing it to run away in fear. (Should have been an opposed roll against its willpower, but it was 11pm and time to go home).<br /> <br /> They leave via the gateway. Mission accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 03-20-2017, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T19:42:56-07:00","id":1071873,"title":"","content":"In some chat roleplay, some of the players have announced some downtime intentions. <br /> Arnold (Void Engineers) is planning to use Mind to not sleep, pull an all-nighter at the lab to process the data they collected. He is going to try to talk the others into coming back with him. (He secretly plans to spike the coffee with nanomachines that serve as his Mind Sphere focus so he can read them, telepathically and track them with Correspondence). <br /> <br /> Dick (Cult of Ecstasy), who has smoked a somewhat ridiculous amount of weed to make his Mind spells work, wants to stop for burritos. And ice cream. The anomaly is in a very rural area (National Forestland and a Superfund site), but there's a town with a Sonic on their way to Tallahassee. They decide to stop at Sonic. <br /> <br /> First order of business at the start of the next game session is to decide whether they're going to keep working or go home and sleep. The Traditions mages have been given lodging in the only thing that Driftwood has access to for free\u2014a FEMA trailer in the trailer park where the displaced residents from the ruined town are living. The trailer park is a shithole of despair. <br /> <br /> Kia (Order of Hermes) and Dick both asked to use Prime to &quot;wash&quot; the resonance of their trailer to make a good meditation sanctum. This was a good call, because the place is bogged down with negative vibes from the Syndicate who provided the trailer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T20:20:33-07:00","id":1071882,"title":"","content":"Dramatis Personae update<br /> <br /> <b>0fe1:a</b> \u2014Familiar/Companion<br /> 0fe1:a (pronounced &quot;Ophelia&quot;) is Oliver's familiar. She's a free AI. Three dots in a Background buys a pretty good AI companion and it took some back-and-forth with Oliver's player about what she does. He carries her around in a mini tablet, but she can live in his implant or free out on the web.<br /> <br /> <b>Mister Glass</b> (NPC)\u2014New World Order<br /> Mr. Glass is a Man in Black. His official job title is &quot;Information security director&quot; of the amalgam. He's a gigantic man who exists to intimidate. Is he helping Karen, or is he reporting her collusion with the Reality Deviants to Control? Glass is secretly (players don't know this at all) a member of the Harbingers of Avalon.<br /> <br /> <b>Brenda McKinnon</b> (NPC)\u2014Extraordinary Citizen, Syndicate<br /> Brenda is the office secretary. She runs everyone's payroll, routes requisitions to the right place, answers the phones, etc. She's everyone's mom at the office. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Surprisingly, the players really latched onto her and interacted with her much more than I was expecting. Unexpected, but I'm super stoked about it because she gets important later and I was worried that what happens would seem like it comes out of nowhere. Instead, they already seem to really care about her. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Ami el-Haddad</b> (NPC)\u2014Progenitors<br /> Ami is a Technocracy trauma surgeon. The Driftwood Institute has acted as a &quot;dispatch center&quot; cover for operations inside the anomaly and her medical expertise has been needed. She is from Iran. The Technocracy's hold on the government is shaky to nonexistent since the election and it's entirely possible that ICE may try to deport her.<br /> <br /> Former Sheriff <b>Bule Jackson</b> (Larry)\u2014Changeling<br /> The rural sheriff was a changeling; until he lost the election last November. He's been drinking a lot and spending time at a stripclub, where he's met a muse who is helping him find his Glamour. This is Larry's emergency backup character in case Arnold gets killed. This is silly and unnecessary since, a) Arnold is the most cowardly PC I've ever seen in any RPG, and b) as GM, I have no intention of killing Arnold until I've turned him barabbi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 04-01-2017, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:37:58-07:00","id":1072811,"title":"","content":"Season 1, Episode 2 <br /> <br /> Scene 1<br /> Starting right from the end of the last episode. We discuss what we learned from the last episode. Arnold's (Void Engineers. Research &amp; Execution) player hilariously translated everything into Technobabble as Dick (Cult of Ecstasy) explained it. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Roleplay XP granted</span>. <br /> The characters end up splitting up. Robert (Hermetic, House Ngoma) heads to his apartment or crashpad at the town with the Zimbabwean refugees (Robert's player had a cold and wasn't gaming tonight). Dick goes back to the lab with Grover (Progenitors). Kia (Hermetic, House Xaos) goes back to the accommodations that Driftwood got for him, a FEMA trailer in a hurricane refugee camp. Arnold brews some coffee and spikes it with nanoparticles, his Mind spell focus. They didn't indicate they weren't drinking it, so I'm assuming that Dick and Grover are now susceptible to Arnold's Mind Sphere Effects. <br /> <br /> Scene 2<br /> Kia uses Prime to wash the Resonance out of the FEMA trailer to make it into a ritual space. It's full of bad Technocracy mojo. It's also highly susceptible to Correspondence scrying, but he doesn't find a specific listening device (&quot;it's the microwave&quot;). He resigns himself to the possibility that the Technocracy is watching him and starts a ritual to make a repellant that will ward the chigger spirits off of him. He botches the second roll and the bug spray trinket he's making is spoiled. He is the only PC who gets a good night sleep before shit goes down. <br /> <br /> Scene 3<br /> The sun rises and the group at the lab are still awake working on their data and debriefing. Dick isn't able to meditate here (bad Techno-mojo), but he tries to help out. Mr. Glass (NWO) comes to work and tells Grover that he needs to get Dick out of here because the supervisors from the Symposium are coming for a surprise meeting today. Dick drives back to the FEMA trailer. <br /> <br /> At the FEMA trailer, a neighbor knocks on the door asking what drugs they're selling. (He figured that two guys moving in are a gay couple, but yesterday he saw three guys, thus, meth lab). Kia turns him down, but Dick invites him in and they get high together. I hadn't meant for this scene to go on as long as it did, but it allowed a great opportunity for a plot exposition of how the evacuation of Pryor, Florida happened after the hurricane. Dick uses some Mind magick to help him recall details and he works through some of his trauma from the even that led to his PTSD. <br /> <br /> Scene 4<br /> The Symposium arrives. Arnold's supervisor from Research &amp; Execution tells him that budget cuts and internal shifts in power in the Void Engineers are going to result in his research being less and less supported. Arnold counters with the argument that an extradimensional incursion should be high priority, but he's told they take it seriously, but it's above his head. Arnold spends the rest of the scene selling out Karen and Grover telling of their treason in colluding with Reality Deviants. (This has a bit less traction then it should, as Karen has connections and alliances that Arnold doesn't know about. This is going to become a factor soon, though). <br /> Grover's research coordinator at the Symposium is getting pressure from the Syndicate to get a marketable product from his research as soon as possible. <br /> Oliver's former squad leader tells him that he has been on light duty and observation long enough and it's time to come back to his old marine unit. Oliver tells him he's fine with that, but he really isn't. <br /> <br /> (Spoiler alert: The PCs' obsession with closing the anomaly is pretty much just them. The Syndicate thinks the anomaly can be profitable if it were in a more optimal location, so they secretly don't want Driftwood to close this one before they learn how to open another one!) <br /> <br /> Scene 5<br /> There is no food in the FEMA trailer. Kia and Dick decide to go to the Food Lion to stock the fridge. As they pass an intersection, their mystickal instincts kick in (two and four successes on Awareness, respectively) and they discover a street that should be a loop, but has &quot;One Way/Do Not Enter&quot; signs on both ends of the street and strong Mind effects directing them to not notice it. They, of course, investigate. They find a subdivision with abandoned, half-finished McMansions and at the back of the circle, a path into the woods. There they find a swimming hole of crystal clear water and indescribably beauty. There is a manatee swimming. Kia with Prime sight finds it to be a powerful node. Dick scans with Mind and learns there are sentient minds here, but he can't find them (They joke, &quot;It's the manatee!&quot; but the manatee is a selkie, so indeed, they're right.) Dick strips nekkid and swings out on the rope swing and swims. Kia meditates in a more dignified manner. They charge their avatars with Quintessence in this way. (They got lucky this time and nobody was home. Once the selkie reports to the rest of the Freehold that they were trespassed upon, they're not going to leave it unattended again). <br /> <br /> Note, at this point Kia and Dick still haven't eaten anything. <br /> <br /> Scene 6<br /> Karen and the Void Engineer major have an argument and Karen comes storming out of her office. She orders her team to get suited up to go back into the anomaly and they contact the &quot;consultants&quot; on their burner phones to meet them at the Cracker Barrel near the anomaly. Kia and Dick are excited about this, as they are really hungry. They are closer, so they get to the Cracker Barrel first and Kia tries to order vegan with no success, or even understanding from the elderly waitress. (A half-hour side-conversation about Cracker Barrel worthy of No Context Games ensued). <br /> The Void Engineer marines tried one last time to sanitize the anomaly with overwhelming brute force without involving Driftwood. Karen is going to stop them, and rescue what survivors there might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:11:50-07:00","id":1072832,"title":"","content":"Season 1, Episode 2<br /> Scene 7<br /> It is night by the time they get there. They get lost trying to find the gateway and Arnold discovers that the event horizon has moved almost a quarter mile. He is surprised and alarmed by this. <br /> Inside the barrier are two humvees about 300 yards inside and about a half mile in they can see a firefight going on. The whispers are loud, but everyone passes their Willpower checks. They make a break for the humvees. Dick uses Mind to shield them from the whispers. They drive across the grassy estuary. It's tough driving. <br /> Kia sees a cyborg in the headlights and Arnold, sensing with Mind that he's under the influence of the whispers urges Kia to run him down. He does so with a string of ten-agains resulting in damage equal to &quot;remember that scene in Robocop?&quot; <br /> <br /> When they come upon the last survivors, they're trapped on the roof of a shack with their comrades possessed by the voices in their heads. Oliver sprays them with machinegun fire and in the next two turns puts down two. Kia gets out and creates a sigil circle that should pin one in place if it tries to step inside it. One attacks him and it does. The possessed marine falls to his knees and cannot stand. (Prime 2, Forces 2, Correspondence 2 opposing Strength). <br /> Meanwhile, in the other humvee, Grover, Karen and Dick see a giant looming shadow just outside their light. He swerves to see it and it is a wild boar the size of a Ryder truck. It goes to charge them. Dick tries to put it to sleep with Mind. It almost works. A turn later he tries again and it gets a net four successes to resist on a Willpower roll so it's just enraged now. (This is twice now that they've been faced with a wyld chimera and without knowing it, did exactly the right thing by attacking it with Mind Sphere instead of attacking it with force). <br /> <br /> As they flee down the field, Kia gets stupid successes on Drive and gets out ahead of Grover. The characters in Kia's humvee plan to guide it outside of the gateway in hopes to emphasize the magnitude of the threat that the zone represents. However, the boar gore's Grover's humvee and deals a fistful of damage dice to the person in the passenger seat (Karen). The humvee door soaks three and she soaks one so she only takes five health levels. She's got a broken hip and is bleeding badly.<br /> <br /> The boar is apparently satisfied with its revenge and doesn't pursue. <br /> <br /> In the real world, it was 11pm and we ended the scene there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T14:28:14-07:00","id":1074867,"title":"","content":"Summary of chat roleplay:<br /> \u2022 Arnold is planning to petition the Symposium to take over the role of &quot;acting director.&quot; The only other candidate is Mister Glass, who isn't a scientist, so he's going to argue that he's not a good fit to run a research facility. <br /> \u2022 Arnold receives a signal from the telemetry repeater. It's a voice reading an endless string of random numbers\u2014a numbers station. <br /> \u2022 Arnold begins a Procedure (ritual) to try to lock onto the location of the whispers (or &quot;theta wave activity that result in auditory hallucinations&quot;). He started this in the last scene and is trying to map where it comes from. <br /> \u2022 I decided the nanomachines have a limited duration so I had Arnold roll Intelligence+Science. Arnold rolled eight successes so the nanomachines inside Dick and Grover are effectively permanent. <br /> \u2022 Arnold is trying to send Grover for re-education as his logic is compromised by exposure to Reality Deviants.<br /> \u2022 Kia doesn't trust any of the Technocracy except for Karen. He's planning to actively sabotage Arnold's gear whenever the opportunity presents itself. <br /> \u2022 Dick plans to visit Karen in the hospital. He and Grover are planning to sneak her some hallucinogenic brownies (and I think these players may have taken this past the point of plausibility to the point of silliness and it's time to dial things back a bit). <br /> \u2022 Next episode will take place in Jacksonville, headquarters of the local Symposium and the trauma center that Karen was airlifted to. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T03:31:57-07:00","id":1080805,"title":"","content":"Recap:<br /> Inside the zone, Karen is grievously wounded.<br /> They notice that two of the three survivors look identical.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 0</b>:<br /> While they wait for the helicopter to airlift their survivors to a hospital, Major Janusz of the Void Engineers Border Corps gets very upset and starts blustering about where his platoon is. Kia gets annoyed by this guy and draws a sigil on his hand and shows it to the Major, turning his volume down (Forces 2, cancelling the sound of his voice). They see him mouth &quot;Who the f\u2014 is that guy?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is the point at which Arnold snaps.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 1</b>: Later that night/next morning, Grover and Oliver drive in Dick's car (a VW Westfalia with a mismatched red door and &quot;All Acts of Love &amp; Pleasure Are My Rituals&quot; and &quot;Visualize Whirled Peas&quot; bumper stickers) to Jacksonville, where Karen is hospitalized. Robert drives himself. Kia drives himself. Arnold stays home at the lab.<br /> <br /> Kia arrives first and Karen is sedated but is alert enough to praise Kia for being the most stubborn person she's ever met and that he needs to talk to Oliver and get to the center of the zone, where it all began.<br /> <br /> Kia tries using some magick and Karen stops him and tells him he should leave right away. He does and he sees two men in black suits and sunglasses come out of the elevator just as he's leaving.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 2</b>: Arnold conference calls in to the Symposium and talks to the Director, a Syndicate VP named Rochester Stoneham III. He convinces him to make him Acting Director while Karen is incapacitated. He starts telling VP Stoneham of all of Karen's improprieties and trafficking with Reality Deviants. Stoneham answers by being annoyed that this call is still going on.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 3:</b> Dick, Oliver, and Grover arrive. The Men in Black are already in Karen's room when they get there. Dick messes with them, offering them a Snickers bar he got at the gift shop downstairs. They have no sense of humor and stare them down.<br /> <br /> Dick tries something with Mind to act as pain management and Karen stops him, whispering in his ear, &quot;Don't. There are thaumatometers in here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Outside in the corridor, Robert hears &quot;Hungry!&quot; and using Spirit sight locates an egg sack the size of a beach ball just across the Gauntlet of that bug spirit they'd found when they were inside the zone. He tells the others. Grover, who is somewhat credentialed at this hospital, checks in on the Void Engineer Border Corps marines who have been been here for weeks. One has died, but three more survive. Robert can see that the bug inside of them has grown and is going to claw its way out and lay eggs (the hospital has been treating it as an aggressive tumor and radiating it, which has suppressed its growth rate). Robert thinks he can treat the patients, but they're going to need to do it someplace outside of where the thaumatometers can detect magick so they don't get caught.<br /> <br /> The rest of the adventure is a heist, but instead of stealing, they're going to cast an exorcism on some Technocracy.<br /> <br /> For some reason, Dick calls Arnold on his burner phone and outlines exactly what they're planning to do. Arnold calls the Symposium.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(At this point, if we'd been playing with the canonical Technocracy, we'd be TPKing in about 15 minutes. I'm not entirely prepared as a GM for this and, not willing to give up on all of my campaign planning, I'm forced to punt).</span><br /> <br /> There aren't currently any Sanitation troops available on standby. The local Symposium is still reeling from their recent TPK.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026more when I have time to type it out\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 04-19-2017, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:14:38-07:00","id":1081232,"title":"","content":"<b>Scene 4: The Heist</b><br /> Oliver's familiar 0fe1:a hacks the building wiring schematics and finds all the places without thaumatometers. The family meeting room in hospice on the top floor, and the chapel on the 3rd floor. They decide to have the exorcism in the chapel.<br /> Oliver hacks the computer and finds the three surviving Border Corps marines and fakes a doctor's orders for\u2026ummm, let's see\u2026 &quot;Spiritual Counseling (Group)&quot;. Dick puts on some bullshit about doing a religious ceremony for the patients and asks the nurses to have someone transfer the patients (with all their machines and IVs and stuff) to the chapel.<br /> <br /> They didn't think to check the chapel beforehand. Reverend Dave meets them at the chapel. Kia tells him the patients are Bah\u00e1'i so they need specific rituals Dave doesn't know. Dave isn't that bright apparently because he outright botches his half of an opposed Subterfuge roll. He tells them that the chapel is available until 3pm and leaves. That should be plenty of time. It is just after noon.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 5: Healing</b><br /> They begin the ceremony. This is a multi-paradigm, multi-mage cooperation involving Robert using Solomonic sigils and ceremony to reduce the Gauntlet value enough to pierce it (Spirit 2), Kia firing a laser beam from his sigil-enchanted LED flashlight (Prime 2, Forces 2), Robert redirecting and shunting the laser through the Gauntlet (Forces 2, Spirit 2), while Grover used his advanced surgical techniques and medical knowledge to stabilize their vital signs (Life 3). The first one goes well; these aren't particularly strong spirits so it doesn't take much damage to burn them to death. Robert, however, starts running out of Quintessence to spend on the ritual. He fails a Gauntlet roll. Grover fails a Medicine roll and they have a scare where they have to stabilize a patient. They finish with their second patient at about 1:45 and start on the third.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 6: Things start heading South</b><br /> Remember how the chapel was available until 3:00? <i>At</i> 3pm, is inpatient Malik Brown's 8th birthday party; his entire class is coming to the hospital to his party. At 2:00, Malik's grandmother, Linda, knocks on the chapel door with decorations (including a poop emoji pi\u00f1ata) to put up to get ready for the party. She is quite upset that the room isn't available as was promised. Dick goes out to try to talk to her, and Gramma Linda confronts him about smelling like pot smoke. Dick insists it's just incense, but Gramma Linda wasn't born yesterday. &quot;It had better not smell like that when I get back here.&quot; She leave to go find Reverend Dave. At this point the PCs put the healing on hold to open the windows and use Forces to blow the smoke out of the room (incurring more Paradox. They've used up their coincidences by now and everything is Vulgar). They resume the ritual and heal the last patient at 2:30 just as they go to leave, they spot the two Men in Black coming down the corridor. &quot;Hey you, stop!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 7: Really, Really South</b><br /> Robert and Dick flee through a fire door and head upstairs to kill the egg sack before they get caught. Oliver stands his ground and blocks the door; once one gets to him Oliver puts one Man in Black into a chokehold. (Note to self: don't fight Oliver; he's a total badass). Grover then makes a serious mistake\u2014he tries to inject the other Man in Black with a tranquilizer. Okay, interesting choice, roll Strength+Melee: One die. Strength \u2022 Melee \u2013. Against an NWO field agent.<br /> <br /> This does not end well for Grover. The resulting Melee was six successes in favor of the Man in Black.<br /> &quot;Grover, He put his hands on you and the floor hits you in the face. You're not sure what happened between those two events.&quot;<br /> Oliver shoots the one grappling Grover with a taser.<br /> <br /> real world time 10:45. Time to go home.<br /> <br /> Next session: Grover and Oliver spend some time in Room 101.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 04-19-2017, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T17:13:14-07:00","id":1086389,"title":"","content":"<b>Between session roleplay</b><br /> <br /> Flashback: 4 weeks ago<br /> <b>Grover</b> (Progenitors) is asked to lunch by a colleague, Dakota. They engage in idle chat, but the colleague slides a note to Grover casually &quot;Can you hold onto something for me? Take the straw out of your drink if you will.&quot; Grover agrees without saying anything. Dakota discreetly slips a micro hard drive into a takeout container and gives it to Grover, &quot;Here, you finish these chicken fingers.&quot; Grover puts the hard drive in the back of a cabinet in his lab. <br /> <br /> <b>Arnold</b> (Void Engineers) is now Acting Director. He is trying desperately to escalate what he sees as a world-ending catastrophe up the chain of command in the Void Engineers, going above the local Symposium to whomever will listen. The voiceless powers-that-be from his anonymous whistleblowers' deaddrop are listening and prod him for more updates. Eventually, he gets the hint that no one is coming to help him and he changes his approach <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(that only took three game sessions)</span>. <br /> <br /> Flash-forward: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">We did this over chat since it's toward the end of the semester and Grover's player has a lot of grading to do</span><br /> Grover finds himself seated in the only chair in a soundproof, otherwise empty room. He is informed that since he has engaged in &quot;non-evidence-based practices&quot; that he is going to receive some supplemental education on using sound scientific medicine. This is probably going to be unpleasant for him. <br /> Since he's been taking a lot of drugs, at the end of this, Grover is also going to be given a vaccine making him immune to all narcotics and hallucinogens. This is meant to cure his addiction, but ultimately it's going to, I expect, worsen his addiction to fae glamour, which, as a Technocracy goon, is going to be difficult for him to acquire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:13:36-07:00","id":1086428,"title":"","content":"<b>Season 1, Episode 4</b><br /> Cliffhanger resolution<br /> <b>Robert</b> (Order of Hermes) and <b>Dick</b> (Cult of Ecstasy) run upstairs to the 5th floor, where the egg sack was hiding, just outside the Gauntlet in the Near Umbra. Outside of one of the Void Engineer's rooms is another young man in a black suit with an earpiece. He asks, &quot;Where is John Willoughby? The patient from this room, is he dead?&quot; The guy sounds frantic. Dick tells him that the patient is in a group therapy session and will be back in a few minutes. They guy looks relieved, but before he can really respond, he puts his finger to his earpiece and rushes off down the stairs. They dispatch the egg sack without further incident. <br /> <br /> <b>Oliver</b> (Iteration X) is brawling with two Men in Black and winning. A third guy (the guy who was just talking to Robert and Dick) bursts through the door knocks Oliver down and the three dogpile on him and the fight is over. <br /> <br /> <b>Kia</b> (Order of Hermes) is in the chapel with the three Void Engineers, now healed from their spirit possession. Kia decides to avoid the scrum in the hallway and climbs out the window, (fails a Forces magick roll to jump; they have so much Paradox now it's not even funny), he mundanely parkours over to the awning over the main entry to the hospital and scrambles down. He escapes to his car and leaves. <br /> <br /> Robert and Dick came in separate cars and there's no way to recover their allies from the clutches of the NWO, so they leave. <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 1</b>: Oliver's punishment<br /> Next day Oliver is brought to a Colonel's office for an official reprimand. The Colonel praises his warrior spirit and how effectively he &quot;showed the mirrorshade brigade that they're not in charge.&quot; The Colonel tries to recruit Oliver back to his old unit, which Oliver declines. &quot;Look, this whole Florida thing is a hot potato and no one wants to be holding it when the music stops. Why don't you get out of there?&quot; &quot;I want to finish what I started,&quot; he replies. &quot;You belong somewhere where that loyalty will be reciprocated, the Colonel says, (subtlely hinting at Arnold's repeated attempts to get them in trouble with Control for collaborating with Reality Deviants). <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 2</b>: Arnold gets smart<br /> <b>Arnold</b> (Void Engineers) finally gets through to to some Void Engineer directors. They expect a Risk Analysis and some evidence that they aren't just throwing more personnel into suicide missions and materiel into a bottomless pit. Arnold calls the Traditions consultants on their burner phones and convinces them to come in to help him make a plan. This works for <b>Kia</b> (Order of Hermes) because he wants to get to the center of the anomaly like Karen told him to last session. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Finally we get to playing the kind of Mage: The Ascension I've been hoping for all this time</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Oliver</b> and <b>Dick</b> talk over how Dick has been able to block the whispers in people's heads all this time in an attempt to replicate it. Maybe if they have some of the whispers they can invert the polarity of the brainwaves and neutralize it like with active noise cancellation.<br /> <b>Arnold</b> checks on his Procedure he started two sessions ago to track the voices with Mind+Correspondence, with Prime 2 making it autonomously running for the last three days. He got six successes on the roll two sessions ago so it makes sense that he can track at least where the voices aren't and can use that to avoid being where the voices can attack their minds. <br /> <br /> The anonymous whistleblower deaddrop contacts Arnold again (they've been typing messages on parking tickets left on his car) asking for an update. Arnold sends them a message blowing them off\u2014<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">he's finally getting who his allies really are.</span> <br /> <br /> they also use Forces rituals to create mufflers for the four ATVs (two side-by-sides and two quad bikes) they are planning to drive into the zone with. <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 3</b>: Inside the Zone again<br /> They see the path of glowsticks and the two humvees just inside the breach of the event horizon. Farther in, they find the alligator-squid hybrid, dead, killed by the Neutralization Corps in the last failed attack. They ride into the pine forest and run into a clearcut. There are pine logs stacked neatly for removal and lots of slash (branches, tops, scrub) on the ground. &quot;Are the Syndicate using a time anomaly to rapidly grow trees for harvest?&quot; This is more difficult to drive in and everyone made Dex+Drive rolls to keep from falling behind. On the other side of the pine forest was the remains of route 15, over a decaying bridge and into the former town of Pryor. <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 4:</b> The Lab<br /> The former Technocracy lab is in an old Depression-era WPA building downtown. This facility's charter was to reduce prison recidivism by teaching inmates job skills in STEM fields (also, recruit potential Void Engineer cannon-fodder for their wars in space). They bust open the door and a cascade of dead pattern spiders pour out. Throughout the building, there are dead pattern spiders along the windows and doors\u2014they manifested abruptly in the material world and were trying to get out of the building when they died. The lab where this all began has a large dimensional warp generator in the middle of the floor. They were not supposed to have anything like this. On closer review, they discover that it is entirely handmade out of parts machined on a lathe, 3D printer, or a CNC machine\u2014all tools they were supposedly teaching the inmates how to use. It's missing a piece (Oliver saw him take this piece off and put it in his pocket in the first adventure of the campaign). <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 5</b>: The Building<br /> Arnold, Intern Dan, and Oliver disassemble the dimension warp generator and load it on the ATVs. Arnold finds a scientist's paper journal in a desk drawer. He pulls all the hard drives from computers he finds and looks for any safes or whatever else. <br /> <br /> Robert and Kia walk through the lobby and notices that the beautiful, marble floors are strange. The veining in the marble appears to be writing. It's ancient Enochian. Kia uses Forces to blast all the dust off the floor with wind. He tries to translate it magickally, but fails, so the three mysticks begin to copy the marble tiles with pencil and paper notebooks. <br /> <br /> Treasure: they find three magick items in the lab, a scientist's lab coat, a dowsing rod in a vent hood, and a magic 8-ball in a bench vice. <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 6: </b>The Voices are Coming. <br /> <br /> Arnold's tracking algorithm sees that the area where the Voice can be heard is moving toward them. The mysticks rush to complete their drawings of the marble veins and Dan and Oliver strap down all of the cargo in the side-by-side ATVs. They flee. Kia fails a Drive roll and can't keep up with the others. The Voice catches up and he hears it. We roll now for the ritual they did earlier to reverse the mind control effect. It succeeds and Kia is unaffected by the voice in his head. Kia then beats a roll against his own Banality to beat the Mists and remember what the voices say. <br /> <br /> Dick fails a Drive roll later in the clear cut and gets his vehicle high-centered on a rock. Oliver muscles it off and they drive on to safety. <br /> <br /> <b>Epilogue</b>:<br /> Between the translated genetic code of the fruit, Kia's recollection of the Voice, and the reconstructed marble tile floor translated, they have a few paragraphs of a crazy litany that seems to be behind the phenomenon. The more of this litany they have, the better their Effects can interact with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:20:47-07:00","id":1089080,"title":"","content":"Downtime roleplay:<br /> <br /> The team collaborates to rearrange the marble floor tiles into a single picture puzzle, then translate the Enochian script. This yields a passage of text that tells a bit of the story of the anomaly, but it's also deranged word-salad, so it's hard to interpret. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">They can use this text in their Mind Effects to increase their immunity to the mind-control that has afflicted the Border Corps explorers in the past.</span> <br /> <br /> <b>Dick</b> (Cult of Ecstasy) has a lucid dream that he's walking through a labyrinth made of hedges <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(clue)</span>. At the center is Arnold (Void Engineer) building a Rube Goldberg machine from a blueprint titled &quot;A Simple Method for Closing a Door.&quot; Arnold has been talking a lot about collapsing the anomaly and he's using a lot of door metaphors as he does it, so this is where this symbolism comes from. Dream-Arnold seems frustrated. Dick says he walks through the door and he wakes up, terrified, but cannot remember what he saw through the door. <br /> <br /> The next day, which is after the team collaborates to the dream begins again (roleplay still in progress, updates to come). <br /> <br /> <b>Robert</b> (Order of Hermes, Ngoma) goes to the community center in the town where his Zimbabwean refugees live. In the pamphlet rack are some fliers and pamphlets proclaiming the evils of vaccines. They cause autism. They're made by Luciferian science-worshippers. They're an affront to God. Full of the hubris of sinful Man. etc. They've been handing these things out while Robert was away adventuring in the anomaly. <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is new and I'm not sure where it's going, but Richard clearly created for himself an African-American Ngoma with a close connection to his ancestral Zimbabwe as something his character cares about, and while it wasn't in my original plot, it's on me as GM to incorporate things he cares about into the storyline. This also came right out of the headlines of the paper, as there's a measles outbreak amongst Somali refugees who were similarly targeted. </span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T16:27:01-07:00","id":1101402,"title":"","content":"A long-delayed post from a week and a half ago:<br /> <br /> Last episode, the PCs entered the anomaly zone and explored all the way to the site of the old Technocracy laboratory, where they found the floor was made of marble whose veining spelled out words in Enochian. They found a dimension portal generator (which that cohort of Technocracy were not known to have). They found a lab journal belonging to Kenji Hirata (the same guy they extracted in the rescue mission in the first session). <br /> <br /> <b>Arnold</b> (Void Engineer) disassembles the entire machine that he took from the old Technocracy lab. He finds that it is missing a component. Something circular about 3&quot; in diameter.<br /> Arnold analyzes the lab coat he took from the lab. It has &quot;Kenji&quot; embroidered on it. He jokes that he wants to go interrogate him wearing his own coat.<br /> Me: &quot;You going to cut the embroidery out of it and get your name put on it?&quot;<br /> Larry: &quot;No, I'm just going to scribble over it in Sharpie and write my name over it.&quot;<br /> &quot;It doesn't work. You've never seen Sharpie ink bead up and fall off a surface before, but it won't stick to the fabric.&quot;<br /> The coat is a trinket. It has an Armor rating and is resistant to fire and chemicals.<br /> <br /> Arnold isn't actually able to interrogate Kenji. He isn't working at a Technocracy lab after all, but has been sent to an inpatient mental hospital in Wyoming.<br /> <br /> <b>Grover</b> (Progenitors) is let free from his Room 101 re-education. They don't even give him a ride in the black SUV; they just take him outside and put him in an Uber. His apartment is bugged, so he goes to the office. He passes on the opportunity to go on an adventure with the other PCs, and goes to his lab to get high\u2014it doesn't work. He tries everything he has: LSD, cocaine, heroin, meth\u2026he's immune to it all. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(spoiler: he somehow forgot to try eating the goblinfruit)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Kia</b> (Order of Hermes) hits the library and finds a book of architectural history. The Technocracy lab building was built as a WPA project back in the 1930s. It had been the town Post Office when it was a smaller village. It was built by an architect/contractor team who worked on some other buildings in the area: including a Masonic Temple across town and a train station in Jacksonville which is now a large convention center. A Masonic Temple? That's suspicious <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(players aren't the only ones who can metagame; I added that detail just to get Kia's player's attention)</span> so they decide to go check this place out. <b>Dick</b> (Cult of Ecstasy) and <b>Robert</b> (Order of Hermes) go with him.<br /> <br /> The Masonic Temple hasn't been active in decades. In the 70s-90s it was a bank. It's been vacant since the 2008 recession and is a dump. It's going to be refurbished someday, but right now it's a squatters' shelter. They find some homeless people inside, one of whom says, &quot;How did you find me?&quot; Arnold recognizes her: it's his sister, Penny. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(This is a backup character that Larry created because he was sure that Arnold was going to die.) </span>They bicker like siblings for a moment and she reveals that she's been outside of their lab and saw that they've been watched by men in a black SUV. Her friend Vanessa has seen the same kind of SUV at another Technocracy facility. Penny directs Kia and Robert to the women's bathrooms where they find some more text in the marble.<br /> <br /> Vanessa is a Hollow One who survived the Pogroms of the 80s and 90s (in my canon, the Technocracy and the Traditions stopped active hostilities after the Avatar Storm) so she's very sensitive to changes in Technocracy behavior. She wants to go back there and investigate.<br /> <br /> They drive to the facility. It's been completely abandoned and looters have even broken through the sheetrock to take the copper pipes and wiring. Dick uses Time magick in an extended ritual to rewind time and look back at what happened. This is what they see:<br /> <br /> Grover's friend Dakota has broken into the office to try to log into the server. Her login and password don't work. A black SUV pulls up with a Department of Homeland Security emblem on the side. Some men get out and tell Dakota she's not supposed to be here right now; she's been reassigned. She protests that all she wants is her research. It's her life's work. They tell her the research belongs to the government. One of the strange men makes eye contact with Dick and says, &quot;We're being watched.&quot; They take Dakota into their car. Before they leave, one of the men runs &quot;sudo rm *&quot; thus deleting all of the research on the server.<br /> <br /> Dakota had been working on a bacteria that scrubs spilled crude oil from the environment as well as an algae that turns atmospheric CO2 into diesel. The director of that office was on the Presidential Council for Scientific Affairs but that entire body has been discontinued and the President is no longer talking to anyone in the Technocracy. Since their office was funded by the EPA and the Council, the Syndicate has closed that front down and reassigned everyone to research that is &quot;revenue positive,&quot;<br /> <br /> Grover now has the only copy of all of Dakota's research on the hard drive she slipped to him a month ago.<br /> <br /> The PCs are freaked out that the men could see them and they go to run. &quot;But they know when we'll be here!&quot; <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(they do not, but I like the paranoia)</span>. Instead of Men in Black, some mundane cops show up. Kia casts a spell on the door to make it extremely heavy (Forces 2) and the cops cannot open it, radio the building is secure, and drive off. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(I'd had a confrontation here, but it was later than I'd thought I'd be at this point and that was a clever way to hide, so I skipped the scene, saving it for a cop confrontation another time). </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 06-11-2017, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T04:44:37-07:00","id":1101564,"title":"","content":"Chat roleplay after the session:<br /> They don't get out of the decommissioned Technocracy lab until after 10:30pm. <br /> On Rt 20 between Panama City (where the old lab was) and Tallahassee (where their lab is) in Arnold's car are Arnold, Penny, and Kia. <br /> Arnold gets pulled over by a state trooper who tells him he has a taillight out. Arnold politely claims ignorance and hands over his license and registration. <br /> <br /> The cop says, &quot;Hey it happens. I'll write you out a warning and get you on your way.&quot; and goes back to his car. A few minutes later returns with Arnold's ID with a piece of carbonless paper, he says &quot;You should take care of this right away.&quot; <br /> <br /> The warning slip reads, &quot;We haven't heard from you in a while.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T18:40:11-07:00","id":1102976,"title":"","content":"<b>Season 1, Episode 6</b><br /> <i>Dramatis Personae</i><br /> PCs<br /> Arnold (Void Engineer): acting director of the Driftwood Institute.<br /> Grover (Progenitors): Driftwood's chemist, pharmacopeist, recently released from Room 101.<br /> Dick &quot;DAP3&quot; (Cult of Ecstasy): burnout psych professor. Consultant on faerie phenomena hired by Driftwood.<br /> Robert (Order of Hermes <i>bani</i> Ngoma): Social worker aiding the Zimbabwean refugees in the area around the anomaly.<br /> Penny Layne (Euthanatos): Sister of Arnold. Not officially a Driftwood consultant, but random bystander to their activity.<br /> <br /> NPCs<br /> John Glass (NWO): security director of Driftwood Institute<br /> Ami el Haddad (Progenitors): medical officer of Driftwood Institute<br /> Dan Dorr (Void Engineers): Arnold's intern, Army vet<br /> Karen Reiner (Void Engineers): former director of Driftwood Institute. Severely injured in the anomaly and in inpatient recovery getting intensive therapy. <br /> Brenda McKinnon (Syndicate): office manager/receptionist at Driftwood Institute. <br /> Kenji Harada (Void Engineers): rescued from the anomaly in Episode 0. Believed to have caused the incident.)<br /> <br /> (not attending this session)<br /> Kia (Hermes <i>bani</i> Xaos): master cryptographer, occultist, supernatural consultant to Driftwood Institute. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">At daughter's ballet recital IRL.</span><br /> Oliver (Iteration X): cyborg, former soldier, now data wrangler and code monkey at Driftwood Institute. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Traveling for work IRL.</span> <br /> <br /> <b>scene 1</b><br /> Arnold and Mr Glass fly to Denver then travel to Casper Wyoming to interrogate Kenji about the Incident. The hospital he is living at is comfortable, not a prison. He is watched and cared for, and gets psych treatment, but he's not locked in and not medicated into a stupor. This hospital specializes in treating Void Engineers who have been neurologically or psychologically damaged. <br /> Kenji is working on a duplicate of his machine using the supplies he is allowed. It doesn't work. He wasn't able to perform Enlightened Science in his actual job and was sent here after it became apparent he was disconnected from reality. He appears to be unable to do Enlightened Science anymore. <br /> <br /> Arnold and Glass interrogate him and as he is confronted about the dimensional portal generator he built without authorization he becomes agitated, ranting about the end of the world. It slips that he dreamed the construction of the machine. Arnold asks him about the missing piece of the machine. It is a lens that attunes the energy to a certain frequency or dimensional coordinate. He claims to have lost it. Glass uses Mind 3 to insist that he answer more specifically, Kenji botches his Willpower roll, and gives up the truth. He has the lens with him. It is a milled aluminum circle with compass points cut into it and several pins into which wires were to go, but the wires are missing. He claims it broke in the Incident. They keep the lens, which makes him upset. <br /> <br /> <b>scene 2</b><br /> about 3am they get a text from Karen Reiner: &quot;Bobby Ray died last night.&quot; <br /> Exposition dump which the Technocrats of the party would already know: Bobby Ray is Brenda's son. He is in his early 20s and she has been caring for him at home for the past year as he has had stage 4 cancer. Bobby Ray was a Georgia Tech student with a full ride scholarship when he got sick. Went on medical LOA and eventually withdrew as he became too sick to return. <br /> <br /> Glass asks Robert to help Grover with supporting their friend and coworker in this difficult time. She tries to take care of everyone else all the time, they owe it to her to return the favor so Grover and Robert bring the coffee carafe from the employee breakroom to Brenda's house and prepare for a wake. Dan stops at Krispy Kreme. Ami brings paper cups, plates, napkins. Dick finds out about this and takes the whole thing to the Next Level\u2122 and starts preparing an insane amount of food. What was supposed to be a &quot;Make sure Brenda doesn't need to cook for her sisters and family&quot; turns into a giant impromptu wake. Ami is fasting for Ramadan (yes, Technocracy can be devoutly religious), so she's around Dick's massive banquet all day and can't eat anything. <br /> <br /> Brenda's sisters arrive and they reminisce about Bobby Ray. He was a star football player, chess club, science fair, church volunteer, etc. Some local kids come to the house to pay their respects. <br /> <br /> <b>scene 3</b><br /> Outside, two of Bobby Ray's fraternity brothers show up, Colby and Eckhert. They are hitting on Bobby Ray's ex-girlfriend from high school, who looks a bit frightened. Colby is bragging about his awesome internship where he's working on cool stuff he can't even talk about. Grover comes over and asks them if they can light a cigarette. (Grover is immune to nicotine after his treatment in Room 101, but he still smokes). <br /> <br /> Dick comes out of the house with some pot brownies he's baked. Colby whispers to Eckhert, &quot;Holy shit! Do you know who that is? That's Dick Phillips, a known member of the Council of the Nine Traditions. He's got a dossier going back over 25 years.&quot; Eckhert doesn't seem to believe him. &quot;No really, check it out.&quot; He takes off his glasses and gives them to Eckhert who looks at Dick and says, &quot;No way. What is he doing here?&quot; &quot;I don't know, but I heard back in the old days, they used to shoot guys like him on sight.&quot; <br /> <br /> Grover becomes a bit disconcerted by this and starts to try to intimidate them with a weapon he's built (a Life 3 brown note sonic emitter). Eckhert flippantly talks back to him with some implications like he knows about him. (They've got a VDAS). <br /> <br /> Dick sees Grover with a weapon drawn (albeit a ridiculous-looking one) and he intercedes. He offers Colby and Eckhert a brownie. They take them. The situation calms, although they are clearly unsettled by a Traditions mage at a wake for their friend. <br /> <br /> Penny, whose movements are determined mainly by Entropy magick, rolls by on her skateboard, sees Colby and Eckhert being assholes, and sets off the car alarm in what she guesses is Colby's car (Dodge Challenger with a Georgia Tech sticker and a Darwin fish medallion). Colby cannot figure out how to turn off the alarm and drives off to work on it where it's not so embarrassing. Penny's thing is that she shows up where she's needed because of Fate. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T19:15:13-07:00","id":1102988,"title":"","content":"<b>Season 1, Episode 6 cont'd</b><br /> <br /> <b>scene 4</b><br /> Some of Bobby Ray's high school football buddies drive up and the ex-girlfriend from high school uses that as her escape from the advances of now-alone, hapless wingman, Eckhert. They all go inside where they find the old friends, cousins, and aunts in the dining room rummaging through boxes and albums of photos. They are making a photo montage for the actual funeral, which has yet to be formally scheduled.<br /> <br /> The PCs see some of his high school football photos. That's when the PCs notice something\u2014they had only met Bobby Ray after he'd become sick. They met Brenda at the start of the Driftwood Institute less than two years ago, at which point Bobby Ray was already on LOA from school. He'd only moved back in with her about a year ago, at which point he'd lost weight and all his hair.<br /> <br /> Bobby Ray at the peak of his health looks <i>exactly like the latest model of Iteration X cyborgs</i>. They've met four Bobby Rays already.<br /> <br /> Grover is intrigued by this and tries to get a DNA sample from Brenda's ex-husband to see if he's really his biological child or a clone. This attempt goes hilariously awkward. He also tries to steal Bobby Ray's toothbrush from the bathroom for a sample but has to guess which is Bobby Ray's. He ends up stealing all the toothbrushes. Grover is a creep.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">metagame note: they don't consider trying to find Bobby Ray's actual corpse. I had adventure notes prepared for them to do this. </span><br /> <br /> Bobby Ray can't have been a clone. There's an unbroken chain of photographs from his birth to the present day and a roomful of people who can vouch that he grew up during that timespan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>scene 5</b><br /> As the impromptu wake winds down, the PCs clean up <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(they went above and beyond what the mission parameters were and roleplayed entertaining everyone very well)</span>., Ami asks them if they'd mind coming out and breaking her Ramadan fast with her as it was a rough day and the Driftwood team needed to debrief as a team. They go to town. Penny skitches behind Dick's van on her skateboard.<br /> <br /> They end up showing up at the pub where Colby and Eckhert are. Colby is using the VDAS and some weak MiB Mind tricks to hit on women in the pub. Penny doesn't hesitate making a pint glass shatter as he brings it to his mouth and he goes into the bathroom to clean up, leaving the VDAS on the bar. Eckhert puts them on\u2014it's the wingman's time to shine. As he approaches another poor single girl, Penny steps between them, calls him by his name, and tries to take the glasses right off of his face and embarrasses him. This causes a scene. Robert uses Forces magick to lock Colby in the bathroom. Grover shoots a subliminal message into Eckhert's brain via a cell-phone. Eckhert is unprepared to resist.<br /> <br /> Finally, Dr. Ami el Haddad, full Agent of the Progenitors, hangry as all hell after a long day of Ramadan fasting, gets tired of this foolishness, walks over and gives the hapless Technocracy cadet a verbal dressing down, confiscates the VDAS, and promises to return them to their internship supervisor with a report on how they were misusing them. The manager throws Colby and Eckhert out. Dick talks the manager into letting them stay despite the commotion and they order pizza.<br /> <br /> (Penny is disappointed as she was looking to keep the glasses, but if the NWO knew they were missing, they'd be able to track them, so it's for the best).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T19:19:44-07:00","id":1102989,"title":"","content":"The players got a really, really, really important bit of information at Bobby Ray's wake and I know they don't know the significance of it. I'm giddy with anticipation here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:51:18-07:00","id":1114019,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">So Oliver's player contacted me and is dropping out of the campaign. I'm sad about this, but if he wasn't able to come and have fun with it, it's better. I hope he can jump back into this group soon, as we're planning some stuff with other games (Call of Cthulhu, the 1980s TSR Marvel Superheroes game, and Starfinder, the space Pathfinder that's coming out this fall). This changes the story arc slightly with what I was planning to do, effectively causing the Technocratic Union to deteriorate faster than was going to happen otherwise. This is because the mystics outnumber the Technocracy in the party, and the Technos who are left are about done with the Technocracy anyway. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Season 1: Episode 7 The Machine</b><br /> <br /> <i>Dramatis Personae</i><br /> PCs<br /> Arnold (Void Engineer): acting director of the Driftwood Institute.<br /> Kia (Order of Hermes bani Xaos): Cryptographer, puzzle-solver, consultant to the Technocracy on matters of the occult.<br /> Grover (Progenitors): Driftwood's chemist, pharmacopeist, still recovering from his time in Room 101.<br /> Dick &quot;DAP3&quot; (Cult of Ecstasy): burnout psych professor. Consultant on faerie phenomena hired by Driftwood.<br /> Robert (Order of Hermes <i>bani</i> Ngoma): Social worker aiding the Zimbabwean refugees in the area around the anomaly.<br /> Penny Layne (Euthanatos): Sister to Arnold. Not officially a Driftwood consultant, but random bystander to their activity.<br /> <br /> NPCs<br /> John Glass (NWO): security director of Driftwood Institute<br /> Dan Dorr (Void Engineers): Arnold's intern, Army vet<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 0.</b><br /> In chat roleplay on Facebook, Penny found a cool t-shirt that she likes and orders it with Arnold's credit card, which she stole from his wallet. Arnold goes to work without any money or credit cards.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 1. </b><br /> Arnold and Glass return from Wyoming with the medallion they confiscated from Kenji Harada. Arnold immediately calls the consultants to look at it. Dick doesn't have the right Spheres to look back in time to see what it looked like before it was defaced and the coordinates wired into it were lost. However, they notice there is something odd and asymmetrical about it. They though there were 360\u00ba marks cut around the perimeter, but it's not symmetrical. Kia asks to count them. The circle is divided into 359 equal segments with the tic marks, not 360.<br /> Arnold (genius) and Kia (cryptographer) are aware that 359 is a prime number. 360 makes sense for dividing a circle since it's evenly divisible by many numbers, but why would you divide a circle by a prime number?<br /> Robert has 3 dots in Occult and Belief Systems\u2014this appears Qlippothic, he reports.<br /> <br /> Much discussion about what this means and how it explains the anomaly. <br /> <br /> Arnold tries to order lunch for his staff and discovers his money and cards missing.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 2. </b><br /> Penny orders a pizza with the stolen credit card. The pizza arrives, but the credit card receipt has a long missive printed after the total (where would otherwise say something like &quot;Thank you&quot; or whatever). The receipt is about 2' long. It offers Arnold help, encouraging him to continue to send updates to the whistleblower dropbox in exchange. She hides it and doesn't tell Arnold about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 3. </b><br /> For several weeks, Arnold has been trying to call for material and personnel resources from the Border Corps and other Void Engineer higher-ups. He has left some messages, no one has called him back. He isn't able to get through as these offices are being reorganized and the unEnlightened staff are leaving for other jobs, reassigned, etc. The Enlightened staff are working by themselves. Their paychecks might start bouncing soon.<br /> Arnold wants a generator that thickens the Gauntlet. The person who approves such requests doesn't actually exist. There's a position for such a manager, but it's vacant and the hiring freeze means no one is in that job position right now.<br /> <br /> Arnold gets a call from a Void Engineer manager, Mr. van der Baas. (Arnold rolls many successes to detect subterfuge). Mr. van der Baas sounds frightened. He offers a Gauntlet machine. Arnold is suspicious. The guy insists that they take it.<br /> Arnold goes home to get his credit card so he can rent a Ryder truck to pick up the machine. Penny confronts him with the note and she's upset that she got a delivery order of Illuminati Pizza.<br /> <br /> They go to a restaurant to meet with van der Baas. Dick gets grits (to go, because they're in a hurry, apparently). Van der Baas is kinda freaking out. They try to mess with his memory, but it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Arnold reveals his plan to the others\u2014&quot;I'm gonna drive this thing into the anomaly and turn it on.&quot;<br /> <br /> cont'd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","user":"GogariGlenRoss","date":". 07-15-2017, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T04:32:40-07:00","id":1116328,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I got busy and didn't finish my summary</span><br /> <br /> <b>Scene 4. </b><br /> Arnold is in a rush to get the mission underway; so much so he forgets to even put on his quantum superposition suit. They move the Gauntlet device from the Ryder truck to a Driftwood 4WD pickup. Of all the characters, NPC Dan is the best driver <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(how smart of December-me to make an NPC with dots in all the things players don't usually bother to commit to their PCs)</span>. <br /> <br /> They drive to the gateway/breach in the event horizon. Dan botches his Drive roll and gets the pickup stuck. Kia uses a sigil drawn on the tire to increase the traction with Forces magick and it pulls itself out. <br /> It's raining inside the anomaly. It is very rough going. They pick their way up the skid trail through the clear-cut. There are already starting to be saplings and scrub growing in despite the pine forest having only been clear-cut recently. <br /> <br /> They get to highway 15 and it's much rougher than it was before. The approach to the bridge has washed out into a sinkhole. Rather than try to go around or do any shenanigans, Arnold chooses to just turn it on right here. Arnold is starting to get a bit careless in his haste, so the others convince him to take it out of the truck, turn the truck around, and prepare to escape before turning it on. They do. <br /> <br /> Arnold switches on the machine. <br /> <br /> \u2026and, scene<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 5. </b><br /> The next thing Kia becomes aware of is he's in a tent on a beach. The sun is up, filtered through the colored nylon of the tent. Grover and Robert are asleep beside him. He assesses his situation. He has bruises he can't remember geetting and more Paradox than he had before. He looks outside the tent. There is a young man in board shorts cooking over a campfire. &quot;Hey, you're up! Want some bacon and eggs?&quot; <br /> <br /> He wakes Grover and Robert up. They each have injuries they don't remember getting. They all have lost Willpower points and gained Paradox and two experience points somehow. <br /> <br /> &quot;Did we get Lost Season Fived?&quot; Dick's player asks. &quot;It's more like The Hangover. What happened and how did you get here?&quot;<br /> <br /> Kia asks the man his name. &quot;Oh, man. You finally lost your shine. That's okay, it happens.&quot; The young man introduces himself as Solar. (&quot;Never go with a hippie to a second location&quot; the players joke). <br /> &quot;What happened?&quot; <br /> &quot;You came out of there,&quot; he points to up the beach, &quot;and it was the most radical thing I'd ever seen. We had a wild rumpus here.&quot; <br /> Breakfast is almost ready. He makes a big gesture to a woman surfing.<br /> &quot;That's December. She's been riding that same wave for an hour.&quot; <br /> Sure enough, the woman is surfing a wave that appears to never reach the beach. It's like reality is a treadmill and she could travel in that direction forever without going anywhere. She's surfing the spatial distortion at the leading edge of the event horizon. <br /> To get out of the spatial distortion, she flickers out and reappears 30 yards to the side and paddles her board into the beach. Solar serves some eggs and bacon onto paper plates. <br /> <br /> <i>meanwhile</i><br /> <br /> Arnold and Dick wake up in jail. They're in a holding cell with two young men, possibly teenagers. One, Moog, is wearing a camo Monster energy drink T-shirt with the sleeves cut off, boots (laces missing), and the shape of a baseball hat permanently molded into his greasy hair. The other, Kev, is a skinny, pale, goth kid. <br /> <br /> Arnold raises a ruckus and a deputy shows up. He demands his phone call. <br /> <br /> They get styrofoam trays of yesterday's mac-and-cheese (this is leftovers from the larger prison kitchen, which is elsewhere). Dick tries to persuade the deputy into bringing seconds. &quot;Our last sheriff coddled you people. Not anymore. We're treating you freaks the way you deserve now.&quot; <br /> <br /> Arnold asks what charge they're being held for. The deputy replies, &quot;I don't know.&quot; <br /> &quot;No, that's not how this works. If you're holding me, you have to tell me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eventually, they allow him a phone call. He calls his apartment at talks to Penny, who agrees to come to where he is. Dick, taking the role of &quot;good cop&quot; talks the deputy into giving Arnold his phone. They bring back a manila envelope, he pulls out a waterlogged phone that won't power on, and hand it to Arnold. This is Technocracy issue, so being waterlogged is only a temporary problem. Arnold uses a Prime Effect to charge it enough to turn it on. <br /> They discuss whether they're escaping or talking their way out. <br /> <br /> <i>meanwhile</i><br /> <br /> At the beach, Kia, Robert, and Grover are bombarding Solar and December with questions. Solar is vague but eventually relents and says, &quot;I guess I owe you after last night.&quot; So he takes each of their plates and sprinkles some salt over the bacon and eggs as he hands it to them and they eat. <br /> The sky turns purple. A dragonfly passing by becomes a diminutive woman with dragonfly wings. They notice that Solar has horns on his head like a goat and hooves. December is a tall woman with elongated ears and nearly lit from within with radiance. <br /> <br /> Where Solar had been gesturing earlier, there is a tall, brambly hedge or thick plants and thorns going all the way to the beach and into the ocean. There is an opening in the hedge up the beach leading to what appears to be a maze. <br /> <br /> This is the &quot;event horizon&quot; surrounding the anomaly.<br /> <br /> It has grown again. It's reached the Gulf of Mexico. <br /> <br /> <b>End of Episode 7 </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:00:39-07:00","id":1120732,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">An aside</span><br /> Last year, Larry, who plays Arnold, the Void Engineer geographer, ran a one-shot Pathfinder game which was an epic haunted house crawl. At the center of the house was a Pillar, which was absorbing souls to feed a Old One (Yog-Soggoth, I think) to bring it into the world. <br /> Bryan, Kia's player, arrived late. We knew he was coming late, but he ended up coming even later than we thought; so he missed all of the plot exposition up to that point. <br /> <br /> His first scene basically went like this:<br /> &quot;The pillar is speaking directly into your mind. It is telling you to approach and enter. What do you do?&quot;<br /> &quot;I enter the pillar.&quot;<br /> &quot;Wait, what? You were supposed to make a Will save to resist it.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh well, too late. I enter the pillar.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was the funniest damned thing that's happened in our group in possibly ever.<br /> <br /> Since then, we've used &quot;Enter the pillar&quot; as shorthand for giving in to evil. That'll come up in this episode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T05:25:31-07:00","id":1120756,"title":"","content":"<b>Season 1, Episode 8: The Hangover</b><br /> <br /> <i>Dramatis Personae</i><br /> PCs<br /> Arnold (Void Engineer): acting director of the Driftwood Institute.<br /> Kia (Order of Hermes bani Xaos): Cryptographer, puzzle-solver, consultant to the Technocracy on matters of the occult.<br /> Grover (Progenitors): Driftwood's chemist, pharmacopeist, still recovering from his time in Room 101.<br /> Robert (Order of Hermes <i>bani</i> Ngoma): Social worker aiding the Zimbabwean refugees in the area around the anomaly.<br /> Penny Layne (Euthanatos): Sister to Arnold. Not officially a Driftwood consultant, but random bystander to their activity.<br /> <br /> NPCs<br /> Dan Dorr (Void Engineers): Arnold's intern, Army vet<br /> John Glass (NWO): security director of Driftwood Institute<br /> <br /> Solar: Surfer vagrant. (Satyr)<br /> December: Surfer vagrant. (Sidhe)<br /> Moog: Redneck in jail (Redcap)<br /> Kevin: Emo kid in jail (Sluagh)<br /> <br /> Not present<br /> Dick &quot;DAP3&quot; (Cult of Ecstasy): burnout psych professor. Consultant on faerie phenomena hired by Driftwood. (Larry just moved into a new apartment and is up to his neck in boxes)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Scene 1:</b></u><br /> Last session, Arnold had been given back his phone as a joke by the sheriff deputy. It's got water in it and won't power on. Arnold charges the battery with Prime 2 and powers it on (Technocracy gear is more robust than that). It alerts him that 22 attempts to hack it were stopped (searched by whatever cop tech tools the sheriff has for mundane searches). He has many messages<br /> Immediately, Oliver's AI familiar, 0fe1:a sends him a text message. &quot;Are you there? Are you alive?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes. I'm in a local county lock-up. Need extraction.&quot;<br /> &quot;We were worried about you. You've been gone for three days.&quot;<br /> <br /> Arnold demands to know what charges he's being held. The deputy who brought him the mac-and-cheese earlier says he just got on shift and wasn't there when the brought him in and doesn't know. <br /> <br /> Kevin, the emo kid, tells him, &quot;He thinks you're one of us.&quot;<br /> &quot;And what's that?&quot;<br /> &quot;Weirdos.&quot;<br /> &quot;He's not wrong there. Did we get arrested together?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah. So, can you do anything, or are you useless?&quot;<br /> <br /> At this point, Arnold comes up with a plan to use his phone as a spatial something something and make a warp portal to escape. We decide he needs the phone to be outside the wall and it can make a warp straight outside. Kevin then squeezes through the bars (causing his skull to compress about 4&quot; narrower, which he just shakes off). They hear the deputy returning and Kevin slides back inside. <br /> <br /> &quot;Which one of you is Layne?&quot; <br /> &quot;I'm Arnold Layne.&quot;<br /> &quot;Lawyer's here.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;lawyer&quot; is a man in a black suit who Arnold has never seen before. <br /> &quot;We're here to extract you.&quot; <br /> &quot;Good. We've been waiting.&quot;<br /> &quot;We?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah, I'm with a consultant and two others who have knowledge related to my mission.&quot;<br /> &quot;We're not concerned with the others.&quot;<br /> &quot;The consultant is vital to the mission. And I'm missing three days of memory. The randos might be able to fill in important details.&quot;<br /> &quot;You have all the information we need. You were once committed to finding traitors in the Union. Are you still?&quot;<br /> &quot;I've been submitting regular reports.&quot;<br /> &quot;We've read the official reports. It's the unofficial reports which are most interesting. If we're going to release you, what can you tell us about John Glass?&quot; <br /> &quot;I think I'll just go back to my cell.&quot;<br /> &quot;That's your prerogative, but if you change your mind, have this.&quot;<br /> <br /> From a folder from his briefcase, he hands him a piece of fabric-like material with a circuit board etched on it. &quot;Keep this. Activate it if you change your mind.&quot;<br /> &quot;Will this work for me and all my compatriots?&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure.&quot;<br /> (Rolls to see if he can tell if he's lying. He's not, but he clearly doesn't care.)<br /> <br /> He sneaks it back to his cell under his shirt. He analyzes the circuit board. It's a transporter pad. <br /> <br /> Can I reprogram it?<br /> The coordinates are printed right on the circuit. It probably would be difficult even with your tools in your shop.<br /> Can I tell what the coordinates are? (Rolls)<br /> It's not Earth. It's transdimensional.<br /> Okay, I'll get on the pad and activate it. <br /> <br /> Did I just enter the Pillar?<br /> <br /> Yes. Yes you did. <br /> <br /> Arnold finds himself in a dim room. Feels like a soft, carpeted floor. The walls are mildly luminescent. As his eyes adjust to the darkness, he realizes that the floor is a surface like a tongue, and the walls are some sort of skin, like intestinal lining. He can see veins pulsing inside the walls. There is a door, which is a vertical slit in one wall. It's growing hair around it. <br /> <br /> Here ends the story of Arnold for now. Let's check in on the others\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T18:39:31-07:00","id":1123732,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Sorry. Busy with work and play and family commitments. Time to finish the synopsis. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Season 1, Episode 8,<br /> <u>Scene 2</u></b><br /> <br /> Meanwhile at the beach, Solar and December are talking with the other mages about what they see under the effect of the Glamour enchantment. <br /> The event horizon now looks, rather than an invisible barrier, a gigantic hedge wall surrounding a maze. <br /> Grover tries to take a biological sample and cuts himself on the thorns. <br /> Solar describes the Hedge as a &quot;cosmic no-tresspassing sign&quot; and he's not keen on going inside of it. &quot;Man, anything you hit over that fence is gone forever. But it is making for some gnarly surf, though.&quot; Where the Hedge touches the water is an infinite space so one could ride a wave forever without reaching the beach (as December was doing in the last episode). <br /> <br /> December sits off to the side having a conversation with the Magic 8-Ball that had fallen out of Robert's backpack. Apparently it's telling her about how it escaped from the Technocracy lab. <br /> <br /> The Enchantment begins to wear off. Dan rolls up driving Dick's car, Penny is with him. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(Please excuse the GM handwaving here, I'll figure out some way that this makes sense later).</span> <br /> <br /> With their memories of the last three days lost, they decide they need to go back into the Hedge and retrace their steps and see what happened to the machine and what happened to them. <br /> <br /> The mages on the beach came out of the Hedge to the south, while the portal they had been using before (and that Dan, Arnold, and Dick escaped from) is northwest. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Scene 3</b></u><br /> <br /> The players have been teased with some hints about what happened. Burns and tears in their clothing, Kia's fingers are covered in paint, a missing backpack. <br /> They decide rather than drive all the way around to the northwest entrance, they're going to re-enter the way they came out and retrace their steps. <br /> <br /> Penny's Entropy effect reading the winds of fate tends to square with Kia's Correspondence sense which leads them up the highway inland from the beach. The highway turns into undeveloped area of pine forest with scattered businesses along the highway. They come to a cement manufacturing plant <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(I walked this entire adventure in Google Street-view. This part of Florida is startlingly sparsely populated. This cement plant is really there.)</span><br /> <br /> At the fence is the torn remnants of Grover's backpack, snagged and torn open. The contents of the pack, including several fruit, are scattered on the ground. Grover picks up the fruit and immediately eats it. &quot;It's like Eddie coming out of the tunnel into ToonTown&quot; and Grover gets the first real look at what &quot;The Anomaly&quot; actually looks like. <br /> <br /> Far off on the horizon, Grover sees a very, very tall tree and he insists they go toward it. The others want to explore what the deal is with this concrete plant and why they went there. Kia sees a sigil spray-painted on the side of a building. It's a Forces sigil for igniting.<br /> <br /> There's a crater at the back of the building. The main building is badly damaged. There appear to have been a large propane tank at the center of the blast. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:39:18-07:00","id":1125559,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Scene 4</b></u><br /> They realize why the propane tank exploded as they are confronted with a chim\u00e6ra. Not like the mythical beast, but a Cronenbergian nightmare of a Florida panther, cottonmouth, and goat awkwardly fused together with vestigial limbs. The snake protrudes through the ribcage of the panther, its tail on the opposite side, black and necrotic. A goat is fused sideways across the torso of the panther with the legs sticking out uselessly. <br /> The creature is burned badly, making its skin even more horrifying as the places where the creatures fuse together have exposed muscle and bone. They must have blown up the propane tank in an attempt to kill it. While the mages remember none of this due to the Fae Mists, the beast remembers all too well and is looking for revenge. <br /> <br /> Robert rushes into the cement plant to find cover and to look for a way to use the building to his advantage. <br /> Penny slashes the creature with knives charged with Prime to make the damage aggravated (her signature move) on her way toward the building. <br /> Kia\u2026 Kia goes super-Saiyan and shoves it with Forces 2 rolling absurdly well, throwing it 30 yards backwards. <br /> <br /> Then next turn Kia announces &quot;I'm gonna boop it on the snoot\u2026by which I mean I'm going to slam it to the ground by increasing the gravity.&quot; <br /> Five. Successes. 0, 0, 9, 8, +1 for Willpower expended. <br /> <br /> The beast rolls its Strength to resist the gravity but its highest die roll is a 5. It's pinned in place and cannot stand. <br /> <br /> The sigil which Kia learned as an apprentice appears glowing on the ground spontaneously, encircling the beast. <br /> <br /> Dan empties the Doorbuster (a Technocracy rifle with an underslung shotgun) into the beast's heads. It is slain.<br /> <br /> end of session. will continue next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T05:53:22-07:00","id":1324194,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Massive thread necro, but this is the home of my plot synopsis. My game ran a few sessions longer than anticipated then got dropped from our regular gaming schedule. Then Dick's player moved out of state before it came back around, so we've been on hiatus for two years. He was back in town for a visit so we ran a special session.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Episode 9 </b>(I apparently didn't type up the last scene two years ago, but this was the last session.)<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 1</b>: Dick, along with his new friends Kevin and Moog are still locked in the county drunktank with the brimstone-smelling teleporter pad. Kevin says he can get out if they had a distraction. Dick reaches out with Mind sphere and discovers the deputy looking at Internet porn on the computer and pushes his thoughts in that direction. He leaves to go to the bathroom. Kevin and Moog, who have been in this drunktank before, know that they need to act now, early in the morning, before the rest of the staff show up for work. He squeezes through the bars, apparently crushing his own skull to do so and returns with keys. <br /> DAP ducks into the evidence locker and grabs their stuff, including Arnold's Technocracy-issued pistol. On his way out, he also takes a box containing a brick of hashish. Kevin insists that they hurry, but Moog also comes into the room and grabs a red snapback Make America Great Again hat; refusing to leave without it. <br /> <br /> Outside, Moog smashes out the window of an unmarked sheriff car and they jump inside. He then growls a string of profanity-laden threats and insults directed at the car and its engine starts. They drive off, just missing the sheriff himself coming in. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(World of Darkness meta: Dick has no way of knowing this, but Kevin and Moog are Sluagh and Redcap changelings, respectively. Dick's player missed a lot of the nuance of what was going on, but Robert's player, who has played Changeling The Dreaming got a good laugh from watching this scene). </span><br /> <br /> Dick uses the hashish then falls asleep in the backseat as Moog takes the car down some country side-roads to hide. <br /> <br /> Ordinarily, you need higher Mind sphere to do this, but Dick dreams himself into the Astral Plane and finds himself alongside his comrades, Dan, Robert, Kia, and Grover. <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 2</b>: Grover, still high on the Glamour-filled goblinfruit, looks up and sees the Astral form of Dick and is able to communicate with him. No one else can see this, so Grover just looks insane. <br /> They make their way north from the cement plant. They detect a radio signal that is transmitting the same verse that they found in the stone floor tiles and the voices. Weird. It appears to be coming from a radio tower on their way, so they make their way to the top of a rise (it's Florida, so overall it isn't that hilly). Somehow, the tower is running without power. <br /> Dick and Grover, who are able to see things' chimerical faerie forms, see, instead of a radio tower, a tree extending to the sky. Dick, much more of an occultist than the Technocrat, Grover, identifies it as an avatar of Yggdrasil, the World Tree, except it's a pine instead of an ash. Dick hugs the tree. Grover cuts some sap from the tree and eats it (which the others see as scraping paint off and eating the chips. You know that paint probably has lead in it, right?) Both absorb a point of Correspondence for their efforts.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 3</b>: They reach a massive sinkhole that has collapsed route 15. At the bottom is their pickup along with the generator, lying dormant on its side in a puddle. Dan climbs down and tries to repair it and get it started again. <br /> <br /> Suddenly, the voices, which had been held at bay by the Mind devices Oliver developed, get more insistent, trying to stop them from what they are doing. Not louder, they remain whispers, but Grover struggles to make his Willpower rolls. <br /> Dick, because he is in the Astral Plane, sees the voices in a completely different way. He sees a massive, minotaur-like beast screaming the words instead of whispering them. It appears to have shackles around its arms and legs leading off into the distance somewhere. <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 4:</b> Dan completes the repairs on the device and turns it on. Dick and Grover see a hedge full of brambles grow up to surround the generator to the edge of the sinkhole. Dick sees the minotaur scream and starts punching and clawing at it until its fists bleed. The others see nothing but can sense that the spatial anomaly has returned. Dan gets very excited that there was a positive result and sets about measuring it. <br /> <br /> <br /> End of session. To be continued\u2014I didn't know at the time\u2014two years later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}